message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "thesaurusscience--amt--gsas-visuals: illustrated scenarios for combining AMT, GSAS and SSSOM terminology mappings"
abstract: >-
  Diagram-only companion repository illustrating five scenarios for combining
  the Academic Meta Tool (AMT, n4o-rse/amt-engine), Gradual Semantic Alignment
  for SKOS (GSAS, Research-Squirrel-Engineers/GSAS) and the SSSOM archaeological
  terminology mappings collected in LasseMempel/thesaurusscience. Each scenario
  folder holds a README explaining the scenario, what GSAS and AMT concretely
  contribute, a sketch of a possible Python implementation, and hand-built SVG
  figures generated by a small Python script (no matplotlib/graphviz
  dependency). This repository does not itself implement AMT, GSAS or the
  mappings - see the linked repositories for that.
